  "id": "methodological-triangulation",
  "term": "methodological triangulation",
  "definition": "Methodological triangulation is the use of more than one research method to study the same question so each method adds a different kind of evidence. In this packet, it refers to combining structural equation modeling with fuzzy-set qualitative comparative analysis to capture both average relationships between variables and multiple context-dependent pathways to the same outcome.",
